#: includes/admin/admin-hub.php:155
msgid "Payments that keep running, without disruption."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/admin-hub.php:156
msgid "With many WordPress payment plugins, recurring subscription charges aren't actually initiated by PayPal or Stripe. They're triggered by WooCommerce, the plugin itself, or a middleman server run by the plugin vendor. That means your payments depend on that vendor's infrastructure staying up and working - and if it doesn't, neither do your charges."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/admin-hub.php:157
msgid "With our plugin, there's no middleman. The subscription lives directly in PayPal or Stripe, and the charge is initiated by them. That matters more than you might think - if you ever decide to stop using WooCommerce or our plugin, or if something happens to your website, your customers' subscriptions will keep processing without any interruption. Nothing breaks or needs to be migrated. Your business keeps running and your customers keep paying."
msgstr ""

